# Isaiah Gap Closure Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Close the 13-item Kaggriculture v3 gap list so the trainer runs Isaiah's `scaling_6m` recipe (cadence, critic, teacher distillation, evaluation) on Kaggriculture, qualified on GPU, without breaking Isaiah's Orbit path.

**Architecture:** The reference model is Isaiah's **stateless** `stateless_transformer_v1` (`StatelessTransformerV1`, contract in upstream `docs/model-architecture.md`), never `recurrent_transformer_v1`. `KaggricultureTransformer` keeps that contract: one encode per current observation, no hidden state, a named token sequence with critic value tokens, and teacher distillation over stateless teachers. It changes only the game-specific stems and action heads. Every change stays inside the one canonical trainer (`scripts/run_ppo.py` + `python/owl/train/ppo.py`). Shared APIs are generalized cleanly; Kaggriculture-specific code lives in Kaggriculture-owned files.

**Tech Stack:** Python 3.12, PyTorch 2.9 (BF16, Inductor), Rust/PyO3 native env (`owl.rs`), pydantic configs, pytest, cargo, W&B, torchrun/NCCL on the retained RunPod GPU pod.

**Spec:** gap list in `ops/isaiah-alignment-2026-09-29/results.md` (items 1–8, 11, 13–17) plus the 2026-09-29 review additions (fixed eval seed, model size, uncommitted work, deliberate-difference docs); rule in `cookbook/decisions/recipe-choices-align-to-isaiah-without-owner-escalation.md`; upstream reference `configs/scaling_6m.yaml`, `configs/winner_ce_6m_4x5090.yaml` at `32b3ec9`.

## Global Constraints

- One trainer: extend `scripts/run_ppo.py` / `python/owl/train/ppo.py`; never add a second PPO loop.
- v3 Rust/PyO3 caller-owned buffers stay canonical; no v2 model/collector/trainer code.
- Isaiah's stateless approach: follow `StatelessTransformerV1`'s contract (upstream `docs/model-architecture.md`: Input Encoding, Transformer Trunk, Critic, Log-Prob Replay, Teacher Distillation). No between-turn state, no recurrent or LoRA features, no history tokens. No opponent identity in inputs, losses, rewards, normalization or checkpoint selection. The critic reads only its own seat's observation.
- Isaiah's Orbit path must keep working: after every task that edits a shared (upstream) file, run Isaiah's suites: `uv run --extra reference pytest tests/owl tests/scripts tests/tools -m "not slow" -q` and `cargo test`.
- After Python edits run `just py-prepare`; after Rust edits run `just rs-prepare`; before merge run `just prepare` and complete `docs/pr-checklist.md`.
- **No training, evaluation or model-scale runs on the owner's Mac.** Local work is unit tests and tiny-model checks only. Every GPU run happens on the retained pod and is preceded by a run statement (below).
- Recipe differences resolve toward Isaiah; record any residual difference. Escalate only where Isaiah would break an adopted owner constraint.
- Every material adaptation gets a cookbook record (note + folder `index.md` + prepended `cookbook/log.md`), per `CLAUDE.md`.
- Work on branch `kg/isaiah-gap-closure`; merge with a regular merge commit.
- Out of scope (owner-excluded): BC log-prob consistency check, post-BC critic calibration, BC data-quality acceptance.

## Isaiah's principles, applied to Kaggriculture

The owner requires the plan to respect Isaiah's principles on a different game. Each principle below comes from Isaiah's own sources at `32b3ec9` (`AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, config header comments). The "Kaggriculture form" column says how the principle holds here, and every task must satisfy it.

| # | Isaiah's principle (source) | Kaggriculture form | Tasks |
|---|---|---|---|
| I0 | **Stateless transformer** (`StatelessTransformerV1`, `docs/model-architecture.md`). Each observation is encoded once with no hidden state. Raw channels go through MLP stems (`→ int(embed_dim·mlp_ratio) → embed_dim`) into a named token sequence: entity, player, global-feature, board scratch, actor plan, and per-player critic value tokens. Masked tokens are excluded from attention keys and zeroed. Downstream code reads named `EncodedObservations` fields, never positional slices. `evaluate_actions` replays actions through the same factorization and returns log-probs, entropy and values from one encode. Teachers must be stateless | `KaggricultureTransformer` reuses `TransformerBlock` built from `StatelessTransformerV1Config` and must match every contract point. Only the game stems and grammar heads differ, and each deviation is justified in `docs/kaggriculture-model.md` | 2.5, 3.1, 3.4 |
| I1 | 16 optimizer steps per iteration; `segments_per_minibatch × grad_accum` = 16; the split comes from a pre-launch memory smoke, "grad_accum only as needed" (`scaling_*.yaml` headers) | Same product; start at spm 8 / accum 1 on 2 ranks; the memory smoke may move to spm 4 / accum 2, never changing the product; record the reason in the YAML header as Isaiah does in `scaling_50m.yaml` | 2.1, 6.1 |
| I2 | Across hardware, keep the effective (global) config identical and divide per-rank `n_envs`/spm by world size; "only the hardware differs" (`winner_ce_6m_4x5090.yaml`) | 2 ranks × 128, 4 ranks × 64; global 256 envs | 2.1 |
| I3 | LR schedule is designed against env steps; a batch change adjusts decay/warmup so the LR-vs-env-steps trajectory stays identical (`scaling_6m_halfbatch.yaml`) | Any forced batch deviation must rescale `warmup_steps`/`decay_steps` in the same YAML and state the ~410M-env-step decay endpoint | 2.1, 6.1 |
| I4 | Model tiers form a ladder: GELU, `mlp_ratio 2.0`, fixed `head_dim 32`, scaling width×depth; the name is the parameter tier (6m = 256×6, 5,679,118 params) (`README.md` presets) | Our trunk should sit on the ladder (`mlp_ratio 2.0`, `embed_dim/n_heads = 32`); game-specific stems/heads change only the total. Current `mlp_ratio 4.0`, depth 7 is off-ladder | 2.4 |
| I5 | Winner-distribution critic, value = 2p − 1, gamma 1 "keeps the critic softmax well-defined"; value distillation on winner probabilities (configs, `stateless_transformer_v1.py`) | As in `StatelessTransformerV1`: per-player critic value tokens (here self and opponent, inside each seat's own observation) feed a shared 2-layer MLP, giving one logit per player and a softmax; value = 2p(self) − 1. Gamma 1 is already enforced; returns stay in [-1, 1] via `terminal_scale` | 3.1 |
| I6 | Last-best teacher stabilization: KL(teacher ‖ student) with small coefficients; the teacher always uses the student's architecture and is refreshed in place on promotion; the teacher must be stateless (`README.md`, `actor/common.py`) | Per-slot categorical KL over the grammar heads in the same direction; same refresh-in-place lifecycle | 3.2–3.5 |
| I7 | Incumbent selection: eval vs last best, 70% promotion, separate current/best checkpoints, `checkpoint_last_best.pt` never the primary training checkpoint; 8 replays exported for inspection (`README.md`) | Unchanged selection; raw-bank winners; Kaggriculture replay export restores the 8 replays | 5.1–5.3 |
| I8 | Throughput by default: compiled GAE/loss (`compile_mode: default`), compiled trunk `max-autotune-no-cudagraphs`, bfloat16 autocast, TF32, forced FlashAttention (`README.md`, 6m preset) | Same settings; Task 6 verifies they are actually active, not just configured | 2.3, 6.1–6.2 |
| I9 | Parity-first engine: `docs/rules-parity-coverage.md` is the source of truth; replay parity against Kaggle reference episodes (`AGENTS.md`, README "Replay parity") | Kaggriculture engine parity against kaggle-environments 1.32.7 fixtures; replay export must round-trip through the native engine | 5.2, 7.2 |
| I10 | Docs are contracts: read the mapped doc before changing an area, update it with the change, `just docs-fresh` (`AGENTS.md` repository map) | Every task below lists the docs it must read and update | all |
| I11 | Refactor rather than add compatibility hoops; fail fast with explicit errors; strict persisted schemas; no `getattr`/`setattr`/`__dict__` in first-class paths, use `isinstance` narrowing (`AGENTS.md`) | Generalize shared APIs cleanly (Isaiah's tests guard Orbit behavior) instead of bolting on shims; explicit checkpoint migrations; no silent clamps | 1.3, 3.1, 3.3 |
| I12 | Workflow: `just py-prepare`/`rs-prepare` after edits, `just prepare` before a commit/PR, dependencies via `uv add`/`cargo add`, tracked lockfiles, PR checklist, regular merge commits (`AGENTS.md`) | Same | all |

Where Kaggriculture must differ, the principle stays and only its game form changes: two players only (no 2p/4p mix or player-count adapters); seat-private observations (per-seat critic distribution); grammar action heads (per-slot categorical KL instead of discrete-target mixture KL); the owner's econ 0.2 shaping inside the [-1, 1] return budget; the native Kaggriculture engine in place of the Orbit engine.

