cookbook/references/native-game-semantics-use-v3-owned-buffers.md:41:Adding the vendored crate unifies `serde_json/arbitrary_precision`, exposing a test-only float decode incompatibility in starter `src/rules_engine/generation.rs`. The fixture enum now reads `serde_json::Number` and checks conversion to finite f64; production game logic and oracle comparisons are unchanged. Missing official Orbit fixtures were regenerated with `kaggle-environments==1.32.7` and replays downloaded using `kaggle==2.1.0`; `docs/rules-engine.md` and `docs/rules-parity-coverage.md` record the retained coverage. This preserves starter regression discipline rather than claiming Kaggriculture parity. The retained final `rs-prepare` log reports 155 passed, zero failed, two ignored, with formatting, all-target Clippy and documentation freshness checks; intermediate missing-fixture, decode and stale-doc failures are retained in the final receipt.
cookbook/references/bc-bootstrap-uses-native-replay-features-and-current-heads.md:33:BC quality remains unqualified: the fixed held-out subset NLL reaches0.761 at14,600 updates, then degrades to1.954 at75,600 while training loss falls. This is overfitting on the selected corpus; longer runtime alone does not establish improvement. Best weights are retained. Full held-out evaluation, action-level fidelity and free-running economic behavior remain unverified. The owner subsequently requests a separate half-hour PPO from BC best; BC is stopped early for that switch, so there is no completed75-minute BC result. The separate launch is documented in `ops/ppo-from-bc-2026-09-29/plan.md`. It failed: after 3 iterations and only 6 optimizer steps (KL 1.8894/1.0453/0.3651; win rates 12.5/10.55/3.52% against the BC incumbent), rollout hit a CUDA illegal memory access and rank 1 then hit the 600 s NCCL timeout. The fault's origin is unresolved and it is not a confirmed OOM (`ops/ppo-from-bc-2026-09-29/train.log`, item 7 in `ops/isaiah-alignment-2026-09-29/results.md`). No final checkpoint exists; the BC best and its pre-PPO copy have matching SHA-256. Automatic handoff remains disabled. The planned Isaiah alignment changes the architecture (per-player critic value tokens, possibly model size), so it schedules one BC rerun (`ops/gap-closure-2026-09-29/plan.md`, Phase 4). Preserve the [[../decisions/preserve-the-ppo-recipe-across-bc-bootstrap|PPO recipe]]; do not infer readiness or promotion from these local-loss smoke checks.
