+# Task 0.3 result receipt
+
+Date: 2026-09-29. Checkout: `/Users/poonszesen/kg-v3-codex`.
+Branch: `kg/rebuild-codex`. Starting commit:
+`559a3956b769200ed183ee7d42fa40f59b79b7f9`; initial worktree was clean.
+Scope and stopping condition: [brief](briefs/0.3.md). No training/evaluation,
+model-scale run, remote telemetry session or network request was performed.
+
+## Change inventory
+
+- `python/owl/train/logging.py`: keyword-only close exit code, W&B forwarding.
+- `python/owl/train/distributed.py`: rank-tagged, flushed traceback before teardown.
+- `scripts/run_ppo.py`: failure-aware logger context replaces unconditional closing.
+- `tests/owl/train/test_logging.py`: new offline logger interface regressions.
+- `tests/owl/train/test_distributed.py`: exception/interrupt ordering and cleanup.
+- `tests/scripts/test_run_ppo.py`: logger helper and actual runner exit codes.
+- `README.md`: mapped training behavior documentation.
+- Cookbook Reference `failed-training-reports-status-before-distributed-cleanup`,
+  references index and prepended log: current rebuild contract and evidence limits.
+- This receipt, brief, command inventory and adjacent logs: working evidence.
+
+## Checks
+
+All uv invocations use `UV_OFFLINE=1`; Cargo uses `CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true`.
+Test stdout/stderr is preserved with `set -o pipefail` and `tee`.
+
+| Command / phase | Outcome | Evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Focused pytest before production edits | Expected failure: 9 failed, 2 passed | `0.3-red.log` |
+| Identical focused pytest after implementation | 11 passed | `0.3-green.log` |
+| `uv run pytest tests/owl tests/scripts tests/tools -m "not slow" -q` | 722 passed, 3 skipped | `0.3-python-suite.log` |
+| `cargo test` | 148 passed, 7 failed, 2 ignored | `0.3-cargo-test.log` |
+| First `uvx --from rust-just just py-prepare` | Lint failed: 2 SIM117, 1 PT012; tests not reached | `0.3-py-prepare.log` |
+| Final `uvx --from rust-just just py-prepare` | Formatting/lint/syntax pass; mypy 48 files pass; 722 tests pass, 3 skip; docs-fresh pass | `0.3-py-prepare-final.log` |
+| `uvx --from rust-just just prepare` with `PYTEST_ADDOPTS='-m "not slow"'` | Build, Rust/Python formatting, Clippy, Python/Markdown lint and mypy pass; stops at same 7 Rust failures (148 pass, 2 ignored) | `0.3-prepare.log` |
+
+The focused command selects `tests/owl/train/test_logging.py`, plus
+`test_logger_session_marks_failed_runs`,
+`test_run_training_session_sets_trainable_parameter_summary`, and
+`test_run_training_session_closes_logger_and_skips_final_checkpoint_on_error`
+from `tests/scripts/test_run_ppo.py`, and
+`test_failed_session_prints_rank_traceback_before_cleanup` and
+`test_distributed_session_initializes_and_destroys_process_group`
+from `tests/owl/train/test_distributed.py`, with `-q`.
+
+The three Python skips are two FlashAttention CUDA checks and one unavailable
+x86 quantized backend check. All seven Rust failures explicitly report missing
+fixtures: six need `tests/fixtures/generation/reference_generation.json`; one
+needs `tests/fixtures/orbit_wars_replays`. No fixtures exist in this checkout.
+`REQUIRE_PARITY_FIXTURES` was not disabled. This is an unmet fixture prerequisite,
+not evidence that logging changed engine behavior. Full prepare did not reach
+its Python test or final docs-fresh stages; final py-prepare verified both.
+
+## Plan adaptations and review
+
+Production behavior matches old Task 1.1. The clean base lacks its
+`OWL_ALLOW_CPU_DDP` hook, so the failure test mocks existing CUDA/NCCL entry
+points. `--extra reference` is absent from the base manifest, so the explicit
+owner-provided `uv run pytest` command is used. Tests add DebugLogger coverage,
+interrupts/SystemExit, exception identity, exact cleanup counts and assertions
+through actual runner wiring. Lint required combined `with` statements and a
+single raise inside `pytest.raises`; no production change was needed.
+
+README was updated rather than acknowledging unchanged docs. This is a material
+reusable diagnostics contract, so cookbook note/index/log were added together.
+The referenced superpowers skills are unavailable in this Codex session; a
+native read-only subagent reviewed the plan and diff with no blockers. Claude's
+cross-review is still required before merge. No other worktree or branch was
+modified, and no push or merge is part of this task.
+
+## Limits and review questions
+
+Live W&B/NCCL is untested by design. Traceback output precedes process-group
+teardown but follows W&B finalization; failures in either cleanup can supersede
+the original raised exception (the chain remains). Hard kills and failures
+before the distributed `try` are not covered. No CUDA root cause is inferred.
+
+Claude: restore the missing parity fixtures in an authorized verification
+environment and rerun Cargo/full prepare before integration. Confirm the
+documented failure boundary matches Task 0.3's intended scope. No unresolved
+production-code blocker was found in local review.
